        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(memory-wiki): reject malformed ChatGPT timestamps",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where ChatGPT imports could accept malformed Unix timestamp strings such as scientific notation or trailing newlines, allowing bad source data to be normalized into valid page timestamps.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe import path now only accepts finite numeric timestamp values or canonical decimal timestamp strings. The regression coverage also exercises signed timestamp fallback separately from oversized timestamp rejection.\n\n## User Impact\n\nChatGPT imports now reject malformed timestamp text instead of silently accepting it. Valid timestamp imports continue to work.\n\n## Evidence\n\nCurrent head: $head.\n\n- GitHub Actions checks-node-changed passed on the current head, covering the changed memory-wiki CLI test shard.\n- GitHub Actions ^Guto-response passed on the current head.\n- \node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/memory-wiki/src/cli.test.ts -t \"imports ChatGPT exports with out-of-range Unix timestamps\" passed after the follow-up test correction, covering signed create_time fallback plus out-of-range update_time handling.\n- A real CLI ChatGPT import proof passed on the repaired head, covering canonical timestamp import, scientific-notation rejection, trailing-newline rejection, and signed timestamp fallback.\n- git diff --check HEAD^ HEAD passed.",
